{"label":"1A","direction":"supports","claim":"Public SRA runs tagged NovaSeq 6000 fell 14% q/q in Q3'26, the first sizeable drop in 2026, while NovaSeq X runs rose 28% q/q.","detail":"Runs released per quarter (release date). NovaSeq 6000: Q1'26 457,550; Q2'26 476,113; Q3'26 408,823, which is -14.1% q/q (408,823/476,113-1). NovaSeq X: Q1'26 111,707; Q2'26 118,865; Q3'26 152,084, which is +28% q/q. X share of NovaSeq-class runs: 19.6% (Q1), 20.0% (Q2), 27.1% (Q3). This is one quarter, and release-date counts are lumpy from big submissions. It is run counts, not Gb. It is also an inflection beyond the flat y/y 6000 reading already known.","url":"https://eutils.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/entrez/eutils/esearch.fcgi?db=sra&term=\"NovaSeq 6000\"[Instrument] AND 2026/07/01:2026/09/30[PDAT]&rettype=count","date":"2026-10-12","source_name":"NCBI SRA via E-utilities esearch","source_type":"dataset","quote":"","strength":"medium","why_new":"Gives a quarterly Q1-Q3'26 run series with a q/q drop; known items only note y/y flat and X share of ~27%."},
{"label":"1A","direction":"supports","claim":"Illumina high-throughput SRA runs show the 6000 down 26% over two years, as X runs grew about 9.3x.","detail":"Q3 run releases. 6000: 552,001 (Q3'24), 411,508 (Q3'25), 408,823 (Q3'26). That is -25.5% in year 1 and -0.7% in year 2, so the 6000's decline stalled in 2025-26. X: 16,351, 60,325, 152,084, which is +269% and then +152%. X share of NovaSeq runs: 2.9%, 12.8%, 27.1%. Combined NovaSeq runs: 568.4K, 471.8K, 560.9K, which is -17% then +19%. The 6000 tail is not disappearing in public data, but the incremental growth is all X.","url":"https://eutils.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/entrez/eutils/esearch.fcgi?db=sra&term=\"NovaSeq X\"[Instrument] AND 2025/07/01:2025/09/30[PDAT]&rettype=count","date":"2026-10-12","source_name":"NCBI SRA via E-utilities esearch","source_type":"dataset","quote":"","strength":"medium","why_new":"Adds the Q3'24 anchor (6000 552K, X 16K) and the Q3'25 values, giving a three-point series."},
{"label":"2B","direction":"supports","claim":"Element AVITI SRA run releases grew 11x in two years: 966 (Q3'24), 4,971 (Q3'25), 10,838 (Q3'26).","detail":"Y/y growth was +415% and then +118%. Quarterly 2026: Q1 7,071; Q2 11,750; Q3 10,838, so Q3 was -7.8% q/q after Q2 peaked. AVITI runs were 1.7% of 6000 runs in Q3'24, 1.2% in Q3'25 and 2.7% in Q3'26 (10,838/408,823). The rival is small but compounding. Run counts, not Gb. This is the run-level view that F582/F583 measured in GEO samples.","url":"https://eutils.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/entrez/eutils/esearch.fcgi?db=sra&term=\"Element AVITI\"[Instrument] AND 2026/07/01:2026/09/30[PDAT]&rettype=count","date":"2026-10-12","source_name":"NCBI SRA via E-utilities esearch","source_type":"dataset","quote":"","strength":"medium","why_new":"F594 gave only ~5,000 AVITI runs in Q3'25; this adds Q3'24 and the full 2026 quarterly path."},
{"label":"1B","direction":"supports","claim":"DNBSEQ-T7 (MGI) SRA runs jumped 2.7x y/y in Q3'26 after being flat for a year.","detail":"T7 runs: 12,394 (Q3'24), 12,873 (Q3'25), 35,144 (Q3'26), which is +3.9% then +173%. 2026 path: Q1 15,687; Q2 29,130; Q3 35,144, up 2.2x since Q1. T7 runs are 3.2x AVITI runs in Q3'26 (35,144/10,838). The low-cost Chinese platform is the larger price-competitive rival in public data. It is likely concentrated in China-linked submitters, which is a caveat.","url":"https://eutils.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/entrez/eutils/esearch.fcgi?db=sra&term=\"DNBSEQ-T7\"[Instrument] AND 2026/07/01:2026/09/30[PDAT]&rettype=count","date":"2026-10-12","source_name":"NCBI SRA via E-utilities esearch","source_type":"dataset","quote":"","strength":"medium","why_new":"GEO items (F585) show T7 samples +25% y/y; SRA runs show +173% in 2026 and a sharp H1'26 ramp."},
{"label":"1B","direction":"supports","claim":"AVITI plus T7 rose from 2.3% to 7.6% of five-platform SRA run releases in two years.","detail":"Share of 6000+X+AVITI+T7 runs. Q3'24: 13,360/581,731 = 2.3%. Q3'25: 17,844/489,660 = 3.6%. Q3'26: 45,982/606,789 = 7.6%. The rival share doubled in the last year and more than tripled in two. Ultima is excluded because its instrument string did not resolve, so the true rival share is higher. Run counts, not Gb.","url":"https://eutils.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/entrez/eutils/esearch.fcgi?db=sra&term=\"DNBSEQ-T7\"[Instrument] AND 2025/07/01:2025/09/30[PDAT]&rettype=count","date":"2026-10-12","source_name":"NCBI SRA via E-utilities esearch (derived)","source_type":"dataset","quote":"","strength":"medium","why_new":"First run-level rival share of short-read output; the GEO figures of 0.75%/3.9%/4.5% are samples and stop at human+mouse."},
{"label":"2B","direction":"against","claim":"Rival run counts stay a small share of Illumina volume. AVITI+T7 runs are 8.2% of Illumina X+6000 runs in Q3'26.","detail":"45,982 rival runs vs 560,907 Illumina runs (408,823+152,084). AVITI fell 7.8% q/q in Q3'26 and Ultima shows only 19 runs under the Platform field and 527 under a free-text search for 'ultima' in the same quarter, so Ultima is negligible in public data. Public research data does not yet show a volume exodus from Illumina.","url":"https://eutils.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/entrez/eutils/esearch.fcgi?db=sra&term=ultima[All Fields] AND 2026/07/01:2026/09/30[PDAT]&rettype=count","date":"2026-10-12","source_name":"NCBI SRA via E-utilities esearch","source_type":"dataset","quote":"","strength":"medium","why_new":"Quantifies Ultima's SRA footprint (19-527 runs in Q3'26), which the known list lacks."},
{"label":"1C","direction":"against","claim":"Combined Illumina HT SRA runs rebounded 19% y/y in Q3'26 after a 17% fall in Q3'25, so public output is not slowing.","detail":"6000+X runs: 568,352 (Q3'24), 471,833 (Q3'25), 560,907 (Q3'26). That is -17.0% then +18.9%. Q2'26 combined was 594,978 and Q1'26 569,257, so Q3 is below Q2. This counts runs, not Gb. X runs are larger on average, and the 6000 mix changes.","url":"https://eutils.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/entrez/eutils/esearch.fcgi?db=sra&term=\"NovaSeq X\"[Instrument] AND 2026/07/01:2026/09/30[PDAT]&rettype=count","date":"2026-10-12","source_name":"NCBI SRA via E-utilities esearch (derived)","source_type":"dataset","quote":"","strength":"weak","why_new":"Contradicts the reading in F597 that combined runs were flat across 2024-26; the Q3'24 base was much higher (568K)."},
{"label":"1C","direction":"supports","claim":"Combined 6000+X runs fell 5.7% q/q in Q3'26, from 594,978 in Q2 to 560,907.","detail":"Q2'26: 476,113+118,865=594,978. Q3'26: 408,823+152,084=560,907. That is -5.7% q/q, and the 6000 decline outweighed X growth. Run counts are release-date based and lumpy, and Q3 may be partly seasonal. It is a weak indicator of slowing public output.","url":"https://eutils.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/entrez/eutils/esearch.fcgi?db=sra&term=\"NovaSeq X\"[Instrument] AND 2026/04/01:2026/06/30[PDAT]&rettype=count","date":"2026-10-12","source_name":"NCBI SRA via E-utilities esearch (derived)","source_type":"dataset","quote":"","strength":"weak","why_new":"Adds the Q1-Q2'26 sequential series."},
{"label":"1A","direction":"supports","claim":"A single AVITI submission shows how lumpy run-level data is: five consecutive runs average about 175 Gb each.","detail":"esummary of UIDs 47044467-47044471 (released Q3'26) gives total_bases of 185.3, 154.1, 184.8, 182.6 and 168.0 Gb per run, about 875 Gb across five runs, each with ~0.49-0.59B spots. A single AVITI project can therefore carry a large share of Gb. Gb-weighted shares must be built from a random sample of UIDs, not consecutive IDs. This is a method note, not market evidence.","url":"https://eutils.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/entrez/eutils/esummary.fcgi?db=sra&id=47044471,47044470,47044469,47044468,47044467","date":"2026-10-12","source_name":"NCBI SRA esummary","source_type":"dataset","quote":"","strength":"weak","why_new":"First base-count (Gb) read from SRA for a rival; the prior probe had only run counts."}
